From: Mytochondria audit <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 05:38:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] voom(): give an edgeR-style offset precedence over
 lib.size, as voomLmFit() does

voom() (since 3.68.0) row-mean corrected an edgeR-style offset matrix
and added it to log(lib.size). An edgeR offset already contains the log
library sizes (edgeR::scaleOffset() stores it on that scale and
edgeR::cpm() and glmFit() read it as the log effective library size),
so the library sizes were counted twice: the effective library size
became lib.size^2/geomean(lib.size) times the gene-specific factor,
logCPM was shifted by -log2(lib.size/geomean) per column and the group
logFC by the log2 ratio of the groups' library sizes. voomLmFit() in
this version already uses exp(offset) (NEWS 4.0.0), so voom() and
voomLmFit() disagreed on the same DGEList.

voom() now sets the library sizes to exp(offset) when offset is given
(matrix or vector), ignores offset.prior in that case with a message,
and keeps the offset.prior behaviour unchanged. Help page updated;
adds tests/voom-offset.R and changelog/NEWS entries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TaHntBDKuZJpMAAMenkC44
